  "result": "Perfect! Payment recording is fully implemented and working. Here's what was added:\n\n**src/payments.js:**\n\n**recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })**\n- Records a payment on issued or partially_paid invoices\n- amount must be positive integer (in cents)\n- date is YYYY-MM-DD format\n- Returns ok(newInvoice) with payment added to invoice.payments array\n- Updates status:\n  - `partially_paid` when some balance remains\n  - `paid` when balance is fully covered\n- Error codes:\n  - NOT_ISSUED: invoice not issued or partially_paid\n  - AMOUNT_INVALID: amount not positive integer\n  - OVERPAYMENT: payment exceeds balance due\n- Never mutates input invoice\n\n**balanceDue(invoice)**\n- Returns amount still owed (total - paid)\n- Returns 0 if fully paid (clamped at 0)\n- Works with unpaid, partially_paid, and fully_paid invoices\n\n**Error codes added to errors.js:**\n- NOT_ISSUED: \"Can only record payments on issued or partially_paid invoices.\"\n- OVERPAYMENT: \"Payment amount exceeds the balance due.\"\n\n**Tests (12 new tests):**\n- Recording single and multiple payments\n- Status transitions: issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid\n- Balance calculations at each stage\n- Invalid amount rejection\n- Overpayment prevention\n- Non-mutation verification\n- Partially_paid invoice handling\n\n**Example flow:**\n```\nInvoice total: \u20ac1452.00\nPayment 1: \u20ac726.00 \u2192 status=partially_paid, balance due=\u20ac726.00\nPayment 2: \u20ac726.00 \u2192 status=paid, balance due=\u20ac0.00\n```\n\nAll 137 tests pass.",
